projects.goalsEn:
With the main goal of increasing corn protein content while serving practical production: 
(1) Isolate and identify microbes from worm castings that promote nitrogen, and establish a systematic microbial strain library; 
(2) Assemble microbial communities with strong nitrogen-promoting effects; 
(3) Develop green, stable microbial products that can replace chemical fertilizers and worm castings; 
(4) Reveal the molecular mechanisms behind the direct and indirect nitrogen-promoting effects of microbes from worm castings.
Expected outcomes: 
(1) Multiple green microbial products that can reliably increase corn protein content; 
(2) Efficient methods for applying worm castings to corn; 
(3) Several academic papers, software copyrights, and patents.

(1) Establish a standardized culture/fermentation and chitosan extraction system for 2-3 chassis fungi to form repeatable baseline data;
(2) Establish a transboundary inducer bank and screen out repeatable preferred candidate combinations;
(3) Through Doe and key process control, chitosan yield improvement and DDA/MW batch stability improvement are achieved;

